# Griff Hybrid - heavy-lift quadcopter (4 arms, 4 motors) with an
# engine/generator hybrid powertrain.
# Flight dynamics are a stock X quad; the hybrid powertrain and the B100
# payload/power module are simulated by Tools/autotest/griff_b100_sim.py.
# FRAME_CLASS 1 (Quad) comes from copter.parm; FRAME_TYPE 1 selects X.
FRAME_TYPE      1
# SERIAL5 carries the B100 link, as UART7 does on the real aircraft.
SERIAL5_PROTOCOL 2

# Two 60 V packs in parallel on one bus.
# SITL models a single battery and then fakes battery 2 as a flat 25% of
# battery 1 at the ADC pins (SITL_State_common.cpp update_voltage_current), so
# battery 2 needs pins 14/15 and 4x multipliers to read the same pack back.
# AMP_PERVLT is halved from the 17.0 default on both so the simulated 50 A
# full-throttle draw is shared between the packs instead of counted twice.
# The 60 V itself comes from models/griff-60v.json, NOT from setting
# SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE here: SITL scales motor thrust by (voltage / frame
# maxVoltage), so raising the battery alone multiplies thrust and the aircraft
# climbs away. The frame model moves maxVoltage with it and Frame::init then
# defaults SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE to 60 on its own.
BATT_MONITOR     4
BATT_VOLT_PIN    13
BATT_CURR_PIN    12
BATT_VOLT_MULT   10.1
BATT_AMP_PERVLT  8.5
BATT2_MONITOR    4
BATT2_VOLT_PIN   15
BATT2_CURR_PIN   14
BATT2_VOLT_MULT  40.4
BATT2_AMP_PERVLT 34.0
